theorem nothing-below-one-is-two
  note        A proof block whose assumption cannot hold ends on a closed
              claim said to be impossible, as a contradiction block may, and
              the block then gives what it claims of the name it fixes.
  then for all x ∈ ℝ, if x ≤ 1 and x = 2 then x = 5

1.  For all x ∈ ℝ, if x ≤ 1 and x = 2 then x = 5.
    proof
    let x ∈ ℝ                                                         (K1)
    assume x ≤ 1 and x = 2                                            (K2)

    1.1.  x ≤ 1
          restate K2

    1.2.  2 ≤ 1, which is impossible
          substitute x = 2 (K2) into line 1.1
